{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 62",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/bc3809e55e601738d56be6885475ed442dec1fb3a0d2e19da14be045510f73dc.png)\n\nThe above scatter plot shows the relationship between age and years of experience of a group of professional soccer players. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one player has exactly $10$ years of experience.\n- There are two players aged $21.$\n- None of the players has fewer than $6$ years of experience.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $10,$ namely, $(21,10).$ This means only one of the players has exactly $10$ years of experience.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/209759f5d70fd8587740d1da840f9da838a3c9a055a0d1e962f76c1cd6341fd3.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $21,$ namely, $(21,10)$ and $(21,12).$ This means that two players are $21$ years old.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/753c503d6751363b1c7d2dc449f1c5f11baec159b1e938e8c807938512111750.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, one player has fewer than $6$ years of experience. The dot below the horizontal line represents this player.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/66facd1a0683f420aa2ac3d7bfd54290bdb009850bc66cc7523ee569ec81daea.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
